# Track E1 KNOWN GAP — Guard[Person].greet(5): user equip method through Guard.
#
# INTENDED (per docs/language-design.md §9.3): the receiver auto-derefs through
# `GuardAccept` to the inner `Person`, resolves `greet` on `Person`, self is
# `&Person` obtained via `emit_guard_get_ptr` → prints `35`.
#
# E1 status (this Track): closes the fabrication class as a REJECT — the
# terminal typechecker fallthrough emits `E_NoMethodFound` for `GuardAccept`
# receivers rather than silently accepting and fabricating a nonexistent
# runtime symbol at LIR. That is INTERIM, not final.
#
# E2 (deferred, pending owner design rulings on §9.4 ratification + GuardAccept
# scope): PROMOTES this cell to auto-deref-through-inner and un-ignores this
# fixture. Fix direction documented in /tmp/scoutE_report_final.md.
struct Person:
    String name
    int age

equip Person:
    int greet(self, int e): return self.age + e

void main():
    Mutex[Person] m = Mutex[Person](Person("A", 30))
    Guard[Person] g = m.lock()
    print(g.greet(5))
